                        ],
                        "form": "flamencos"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13881adf-25b5-35a4-bf31-978adeeb6a1a",
                        "entry_id": "35db7561-d473-37b2-affc-edf04724c6ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genre musical à base de chant et type de danse populaires andalous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3eb0916c-c15e-4e25-97bd-a90f05718695",
                                "sense_id": "13881adf-25b5-35a4-bf31-978adeeb6a1a",
                                "text": "Il voyageait dans les régions les moins fréquentées de l’Espagne, à la recherche d’anciennes musiques ibériques, mélopées de faucheurs, de guardianes ou de promeneurs solitaires, plus vieilles même que la conquête par Rome et les chants d’église, bouts de complaintes tziganes venues d’Asie centrale avec la tribu, bien avant le flamenco de la Renaissance ou même le Canto jondo si rarement entendu pur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd52887d-fcd3-437e-b531-c52d25ddea49",
                                "sense_id": "13881adf-25b5-35a4-bf31-978adeeb6a1a",
                                "text": "Les deux enfants sont inséparables et nourrissent une passion commune: la danse, et bientôt le flamenco, très à la mode dans les années 1930."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9bdf8519-b5d9-4871-a5ff-02bf322171b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "35db7561-d473-37b2-affc-edf04724c6ec",
                        "source_sense_id": "13881adf-25b5-35a4-bf31-978adeeb6a1a",
                        "target_lang_word": "flamenco",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "flamenco",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f31c115-6bf6-3632-add8-bf080a1f6e14",
                                        "entry_id": "e1d01722-977e-37e1-abc4-7cbd511e5261",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A genre of folk music and dance native to Andalusia, in Spain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecf7b75a-a466-45ac-b9c3-822d2ac1a8d0",
                                                "sense_id": "6f31c115-6bf6-3632-add8-bf080a1f6e14",
                                                "text": "It's impossible to tell the story of flamenco without talking about Lorca, who found in it a source of inspiration in a lifelong political-cultural-sexual struggle against bourgeois philistinism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9961b86-f645-48a9-84b6-d12eb396fe19",
                                                "sense_id": "6f31c115-6bf6-3632-add8-bf080a1f6e14",
                                                "text": "Among the dancers, who joined in periodically, the outlier wasn’t the Spanish flamenco dancer, Jesús Carmona (in town for the Flamenco Festival at City Center), so much as the New York salsero, Eddie Torres Jr."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a3fdced-b2cd-3eac-8be4-2e903f57571a",
                                        "entry_id": "e1d01722-977e-37e1-abc4-7cbd511e5261",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A song or dance performed in such a style."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32749c4e-bcb7-4f88-93cd-cd4888d1e19c",
                                                "sense_id": "3a3fdced-b2cd-3eac-8be4-2e903f57571a",
                                                "text": "La Niña was so goddam terrific that after a month of singing with the vocal trio, she was singing solo and she was dancing a flamenco better'n a gypsy fireball!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "flamenco",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e82163f-7c41-3910-81d7-321cbc6d4a90",
                                        "entry_id": "8e23b8ec-3deb-337c-a891-5d728743ef56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dance flamenco."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d8cdffc-ae45-4c31-b4ae-a4cc4a13451b",
                                                "sense_id": "9e82163f-7c41-3910-81d7-321cbc6d4a90",
                                                "text": "\"Can you flamenco?\" \"If I have to. How about you?\" \"Love, I can barely waltz. Jive a bit if I'm pissed enough.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "487ec8c2-85ea-445d-8c2d-49020685b623",
                                                "sense_id": "9e82163f-7c41-3910-81d7-321cbc6d4a90",
                                                "text": "Behind them on horseback sat six men, two with guitars, one with a trumpet, and three women also on horses: Nadia, an older woman, and the girl Gus had flamencoed with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
